    "title": "Hans in Luck",
    "level": "Level 2",
    "text": "SC01_ST01_N = Hans works hard for seven years.\nSC01_ST02_N = He receives a big piece of gold as pay.\nSC01_ST03_N = Hans puts the gold on his shoulder and starts to walk home to his mother.\nSC02_ST01_N = The gold is very heavy.\nSC02_ST02_N = Hans sees a man on a horse.\nSC02_ST03_N = \"Riding looks easy,\" says Hans.\nSC03_ST01_N = The man stops and says, \"Give me your gold, and I will give you my horse.\"\nSC03_ST02_N = Hans is happy to trade.\nSC04_ST01_N = Hans gets on the horse, but the horse runs too fast.\nSC04_ST02_N = He falls to the ground.\nSC04_ST03_N = A farmer with a cow helps him stand up.\nSC05_ST01_N = \"Horses are dangerous,\" says Hans.\nSC05_ST02_N = \"I like your cow.\nSC05_ST03_N = It gives milk every day.\"\nSC05_ST04_N = The farmer smiles and says, \"I will trade my cow for your horse.\"\nSC05_ST05_N = Hans agrees right away.\nSC06_ST01_N = Hans walks with the cow.\nSC06_ST02_N = He feels very thirsty and tries to get milk.\nSC06_ST03_N = But no milk comes out.\nSC06_ST04_N = The cow kicks Hans, and he falls down.\nSC07_ST01_N = A man with a pig sees him.\nSC07_ST02_N = \"That cow is too old to give milk,\" says the man.\nSC07_ST03_N = \"Your pig looks young and good,\" says Hans.\nSC07_ST04_N = \"I can trade my pig for the cow,\" says the man.\nSC07_ST05_N = Hans agrees to the trade.\nSC08_ST01_N = Later, Hans meets a boy with a white goose.\nSC08_ST02_N = Hans tells the boy about his lucky trades.\nSC08_ST03_N = The boy says, \"My goose is very heavy.\nSC08_ST04_N = The meat will be good.\"\nSC08_ST05_N = \"My pig is good, too,\" says Hans.\nSC09_ST01_N = Then the boy says, \"Is that pig yours?\nSC09_ST02_N = A rich man is looking for his lost pig.\nSC09_ST03_N = It is missing.\nSC09_ST04_N = You may be in trouble.\"\nSC09_ST05_N = Hans feels afraid.\nSC09_ST06_N = \"Please help me,\" he says.\nSC09_ST07_N = \"Take this pig and give me your goose.\"\nSC10_ST01_N = Hans thinks he is very lucky with the big goose.\nSC10_ST02_N = In the next village, he sees a man with a large stone.\nSC10_ST03_N = The man uses the stone for his work.\nSC10_ST04_N = The man sings while he works.\nSC10_ST05_N = \"You look happy,\" says Hans.\nSC11_ST01_N = The man says, \"My work brings me money.\nSC11_ST02_N = You can do this work, too.\"\nSC11_ST03_N = \"How can I do that?\" asks Hans.\nSC11_ST04_N = \"You just need a stone,\" says the man.\nSC11_ST05_N = \"Take this goose and give me your stone,\" says Hans.\nSC12_ST01_N = \"Now I will be rich,\" Hans thinks.\nSC12_ST02_N = But the stone is very heavy.\nSC12_ST03_N = Soon, Hans feels tired and hungry.\nSC13_ST01_N = Hans stops at a well to drink water.\nSC13_ST02_N = He puts the stone on the edge.\nSC13_ST03_N = By accident, he pushes the stone.\nSC13_ST04_N = Splash!\nSC13_ST05_N = It falls into the deep water.\nSC14_ST01_N = He jumps for joy.\nSC14_ST02_N = \"Thank my lucky stars!\" he shouts.\nSC14_ST03_N = \"The heavy stone is gone.\nSC14_ST04_N = I am free from this heavy weight.\"\nSC14_ST05_N = Now he has nothing left.\nSC14_ST06_N = He has no gold, no horse, and no stone.\nSC14_ST07_N = But he is the happiest man in the world.",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "sceneId": "SC01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST01_N",
            "text": "Hans works hard for seven years."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST02_N",
            "text": "He receives a big piece of gold as pay."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST03_N",
            "text": "Hans puts the gold on his shoulder and starts to walk home to his mother."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST01_N",
            "text": "The gold is very heavy."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST02_N",
            "text": "Hans sees a man on a horse."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST03_N",
            "text": "\"Riding looks easy,\" says Hans."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC03_ST01_N",
            "text": "The man stops and says, \"Give me your gold, and I will give you my horse.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC03_ST02_N",
            "text": "Hans is happy to trade."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC04_ST01_N",
            "text": "Hans gets on the horse, but the horse runs too fast."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC04_ST02_N",
            "text": "He falls to the ground."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC04_ST03_N",
            "text": "A farmer with a cow helps him stand up."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST01_N",
            "text": "\"Horses are dangerous,\" says Hans."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"I like your cow."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST03_N",
            "text": "It gives milk every day.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST04_N",
            "text": "The farmer smiles and says, \"I will trade my cow for your horse.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST05_N",
            "text": "Hans agrees right away."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC06",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST01_N",
            "text": "Hans walks with the cow."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST02_N",
            "text": "He feels very thirsty and tries to get milk."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST03_N",
            "text": "But no milk comes out."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST04_N",
            "text": "The cow kicks Hans, and he falls down."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC07",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST01_N",
            "text": "A man with a pig sees him."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"That cow is too old to give milk,\" says the man."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST03_N",
            "text": "\"Your pig looks young and good,\" says Hans."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST04_N",
            "text": "\"I can trade my pig for the cow,\" says the man."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST05_N",
            "text": "Hans agrees to the trade."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC08",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST01_N",
            "text": "Later, Hans meets a boy with a white goose."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST02_N",
            "text": "Hans tells the boy about his lucky trades."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST03_N",
            "text": "The boy says, \"My goose is very heavy."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST04_N",
            "text": "The meat will be good.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST05_N",
            "text": "\"My pig is good, too,\" says Hans."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC09",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST01_N",
            "text": "Then the boy says, \"Is that pig yours?"
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST02_N",
            "text": "A rich man is looking for his lost pig."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST03_N",
            "text": "It is missing."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST04_N",
            "text": "You may be in trouble.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST05_N",
            "text": "Hans feels afraid."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST06_N",
            "text": "\"Please help me,\" he says."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST07_N",
            "text": "\"Take this pig and give me your goose.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC10",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST01_N",
            "text": "Hans thinks he is very lucky with the big goose."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST02_N",
            "text": "In the next village, he sees a man with a large stone."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST03_N",
            "text": "The man uses the stone for his work."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST04_N",
            "text": "The man sings while he works."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST05_N",
            "text": "\"You look happy,\" says Hans."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC11",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST01_N",
            "text": "The man says, \"My work brings me money."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST02_N",
            "text": "You can do this work, too.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST03_N",
            "text": "\"How can I do that?\" asks Hans."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST04_N",
            "text": "\"You just need a stone,\" says the man."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST05_N",
            "text": "\"Take this goose and give me your stone,\" says Hans."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC12",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC12_ST01_N",
            "text": "\"Now I will be rich,\" Hans thinks."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC12_ST02_N",
            "text": "But the stone is very heavy."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC12_ST03_N",
            "text": "Soon, Hans feels tired and hungry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC13",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST01_N",
            "text": "Hans stops at a well to drink water."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST02_N",
            "text": "He puts the stone on the edge."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST03_N",
            "text": "By accident, he pushes the stone."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST04_N",
            "text": "Splash!"
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST05_N",
            "text": "It falls into the deep water."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC14",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST01_N",
            "text": "He jumps for joy."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"Thank my lucky stars!\" he shouts."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST03_N",
            "text": "\"The heavy stone is gone."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST04_N",
            "text": "I am free from this heavy weight.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST05_N",
            "text": "Now he has nothing left."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST06_N",
            "text": "He has no gold, no horse, and no stone."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST07_N",
            "text": "But he is the happiest man in the world."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
